// LEGACY: no-alias A B C
// LEGACY: no-alias-note A: buffer 'ba' over std::vector 'va'
// MISMATCH, explained: std::vector::data is analysed (its role is not
// modelled) and context-insensitively, so its one formal binds the three
// vectors: their storages are one node. Legacy reads each call's own operand.
